A_576 - Nature has always tried to tell us through disastrous events what's wrong with our philosophy. When disastrous events occur (murders, attacks), it's always because there are philosophical shortcomings or problems that are highlighted and for which we must make changes or find solutions. As far as I'm concerned, I also see in the recent murders and femicides discussed in the news references to a flawed philosophy that was or is still waiting to be resolved, but the same is true for less recent events as well. It's always important to try to read events from a different perspective to understand if there are any indications being expressed. Personally, I've managed to find philosophical correlations with many problems, which I've also described in these texts of mine, using crime stories commonly reported on news programs and national newspapers, so it's also for this reason that I support this thesis. That said, it might still be useful to go back in time and analyze all the tragedies that have occurred to understand if there were any philosophical errors or problems that were somehow indicated, and highlight them.